<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Francesco Maria II della Rovere</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1549–<a href="/years/1631">1631</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/17th-century">17th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Francesco Maria II della Rovere was the last Duke of Urbino, ruling from 1574. A learned and pious prince, he fought at the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-lepanto">Battle of Lepanto</a> in 1571 and later lived mostly in retirement. His only son died in 1623, and by agreement with the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/papacy">papacy</a> the duchy passed to the Papal States on his death in 1631. His library and art collections were divided between <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rome">Rome</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/florence">Florence</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/francesco-maria-ii-della-rovere.jpg" alt="Francesco Maria II della Rovere" width="320" height="378" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Federico Barocci · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Francesco_II_della_Rovere.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
